    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are locked in for today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two elite offensive projections. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) represents our strongest play, bolstered by an exceptional BvP history (26 PA) and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Rod\u00f3n. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) remains a must-start; the intersection of a weak opposing starter in Martinez and an optimal #3 hole placement makes him a foundational piece for our Roto output today. While **Kyle Tucker** shows a lower raw score (58.73) due to a challenging matchup against Bachar, his multi-category ceiling necessitates his presence in the outfield as we continue to hunt for counting stats.\n\nStrategic efficiency remains a priority, specifically regarding our pursuit of stolen bases. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) provides high value today, as his projection benefits from a slow opposing battery delivery that maximizes his efficiency in the SB category. The most difficult decision at the margins involved **Miguel Vargas**, who landed on the bench with a 47.01 score. While his xwOBA remains strong, he ultimately lost out to our starting infielders due to a combination of park factors and the necessity of prioritizing higher-floor players like **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Coby Mayo** against their respective right-handed matchups.\n\nSeveral situational risks require monitoring as we progress through the day. **Drake Baldwin** is currently running as a \"Lineup Pending\" assumption in the #1 spot; should he be shifted down the order or benched, his 57.14 efficiency score will be heavily impacted. Additionally, while **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits from a favorable wind forecast, we are keeping a close eye on any late-game weather fluctuations that could dampen his power potential against Newcomb. With **Jordan Westburg** and **Andy Pages** remaining on the IL, our current roster must maintain high plate discipline to protect our remaining game caps while **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** provide the necessary speed floor to keep us competitive in the SB category.",
